On Tue, 18 Feb 1997, Trevor Hill wrote:

> I have a question about an example lujvo I saw in the reference grammar...
>
> -- dzukla --
>
> It seems to me that if i say for instance,
>
> .i ca dzukla ma .....
>
> that could easily be misinterpreted as
>
> .i cadzu klama .....
>
> -- Could someone clarify this for me??  :)

  I'm by no means an expert, but my take on this is that it's a question
of emphasis:

".i ca dzukla ma" is pronounced ".i ca DZUkla ma"
".i cadzu klama" is pronounced ".i CADzu KLAma"

-marvin

